{"title":"The evolution of the economics job market","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/924608946/0/marginalrevolution~The-evolution-of-the-economics-job-market.html","date":1757480423000,"content":"<blockquote>\r\n<p>In the halcyon days of 2015-19, openings on the economics job market hovered at around 1900 per year. In 2020, Covid was a major shock, but the market bounced back quickly in 2021 and 2022. Since then, though, the market has clearly been in a funk. 2023, my job market year, saw a sudden dip in postings. 2024 was even worse, with openings falling 16% lower than the 2015-19 average.</p>\r\n<p>At the time, the sudden fall in 2023 seemed mysterious—it was an otherwise healthy year for the broader labor market. In hindsight, it seems like the 2021-22 recovery masked some underlying weakness. The 2020 job market had 500 fewer openings than the 2014-19 average; 2021 and 2022 together produced only around 100 more jobs than the 2014-19 average. In other words, the recovery never made up for the pandemic; by this crude logic, around 400 economist jobs were “destroyed”.</p>\r\n<p>…<span>And of course, all of this decline occurred </span><em>before</em> the litany of disasters that have recently hit the Econ job market. In May, Jerome Powell announced that the Federal Reserve—perhaps <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack.com%2Fredirect%2Fd7b00230-3e44-4a68-b063-9ab9861ec11e%3Fj%3DeyJ1IjoiM285In0.FYORq_H-OKLpmdRjBukHHZzTJ6NOFfwRxYngojeKDOQ&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Cfa01e544476f42d199e208ddefb659c1%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638930288685511279%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=pJMSGs9X9%2BJxPiaoNZHJTSVxzWHEMX4T598VfY367Q0%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">the largest employer of economists in America</a>—would cut its workforce by 10%. The <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack.com%2Fredirect%2F6655bc93-5618-426e-9c72-daa87babb4d5%3Fj%3DeyJ1IjoiM285In0.FYORq_H-OKLpmdRjBukHHZzTJ6NOFfwRxYngojeKDOQ&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Cfa01e544476f42d199e208ddefb659c1%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638930288685564279%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=2YojfJ%2FD7WAFvloDL1J460x7Ogs%2Br9cYGgSR0mJAL0w%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">federal government</a> has frozen hiring, as has the World Bank. Hit by the dual threat of fines and looming cuts to federal funding, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack.com%2Fredirect%2Fc4e4dd69-7dbe-4661-a2ba-c80d0992a6c2%3Fj%3DeyJ1IjoiM285In0.FYORq_H-OKLpmdRjBukHHZzTJ6NOFfwRxYngojeKDOQ&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Cfa01e544476f42d199e208ddefb659c1%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638930288685603905%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=AC0bv8r%2BNDX0CeJzfjvHCFLMhlYbKJU%2F6zg4d9PvA2Q%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">Harvard</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack.com%2Fredirect%2F5089ad4a-dbba-4008-aab0-11486f9a5547%3Fj%3DeyJ1IjoiM285In0.FYORq_H-OKLpmdRjBukHHZzTJ6NOFfwRxYngojeKDOQ&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Cfa01e544476f42d199e208ddefb659c1%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638930288685645946%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=vcEIEiWD5jsLnJm0MzLDVDLXEBAGRnNSeZLWnZjsdcM%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">MIT</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack.com%2Fredirect%2F43c23faa-4d00-4c67-8300-ebd787f978fe%3Fj%3DeyJ1IjoiM285In0.FYORq_H-OKLpmdRjBukHHZzTJ6NOFfwRxYngojeKDOQ&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Cfa01e544476f42d199e208ddefb659c1%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638930288685692626%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=WgH%2FPgIHiuKp%2FUkvyPbcMzi0nDpJTlno3j1W38ZFerc%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">the University of Washington</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack.com%2Fredirect%2F41f334f7-09bf-4bf7-85b4-653b108c6bd1%3Fj%3DeyJ1IjoiM285In0.FYORq_H-OKLpmdRjBukHHZzTJ6NOFfwRxYngojeKDOQ&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Cfa01e544476f42d199e208ddefb659c1%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638930288685740089%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=pe3m0iB6eHNdCCtanR%2Byzp34QVQ3pYDXwxtrfSxhcQo%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">Notre Dame, Northwestern University</a>, among others, have announced hiring freezes and budget cuts.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.global-developments.org/p/twilight-of-the-econs?utm_source=activity_item\" target=\"_blank\">more from Oliver Kim</a>, who also offers a much broader discussion of the meaning of all this.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/the-evolution-of-the-economics-job-market.html\">The evolution of the economics job market</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/924608946/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/924608946/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/924608946/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/924608946/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/924608946/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/924608946/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/the-evolution-of-the-economics-job-market.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/the-evolution-of-the-economics-job-market.html/feed\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/commentsrss20.png\" /></a> \r\n<div><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/the-evolution-of-the-economics-job-market.html#comments\"><h3>Comments</h3></a><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/the-evolution-of-the-economics-job-market.html#comment-160961474\">Would you rather have the bureaucracy staffed by lawyers?   A ...</a> <i>by Dismalist</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/the-evolution-of-the-economics-job-market.html#comment-160961473\">How much of this is related to the wider white collar/tech job ...</a> <i>by Naveen_K</i></li>